<h2>Deployment and Monitoring</h2>
<p><b>Serving.</b> <code>predict(text)</code> returns label, confidence, OOD score, abstained flag and top three; below the Mahalanobis threshold the router sends the message to the unknown path instead of a handler. Default backend: ONNX fp32 on CPU, one thread, batch-1{% if srv_colab %}: p50 {{ n('srv.onnx_fp32.t1.p50') }} ms and p95 {{ n('srv.onnx_fp32.t1.p95') }} ms ({{ M() }} Colab shared vCPUs, environment in Appendix {{ sec.latency }}; PyTorch fp32 p50 {{ n('srv.torch.t1.p50') }} ms, p95 {{ n('srv.torch.t1.p95') }} ms){% else %}; CPU latency is measured in the Colab canonical run and filled at publish time{% endif %}. int8 quantization did not meet the pre-set rule (macro-F1 delta at least {{ n('q.margin') }} on both splits; validation {{ n('q.d_val') }}), so fp32 ships.</p>
<p><b>Monitoring and drift.</b> Abstention rate (test reference: {{ n('srv.cov') }} coverage), confidence and energy distributions, language mix against the measured {{ n('eda.nonen') }} non-English, kNN distance to train (PSI or MMD against a reference window), per-intent volume and handler failure rate; weekly sampled label audits by humans, because consensus labelling by LLM judges did not meet its calibration gate (judge accuracy {{ n('aud2.llama3') }} to {{ n('aud2.gemma3') }} against {{ n('aud2.gate') }}).</p>
<p><b>13th-class playbook.</b> Cluster the abstained traffic, label the cluster, add the class at once through the kNN bank (no retraining), then retrain fully, shadow-evaluate against v1 and promote; retrain on a sustained rise in abstention, a kNN-distance PSI alert, a handler failure spike or a new labelled cluster of meaningful size.</p>
