<h2>Next Steps</h2>
<ul class="tight">
<li><b>Verified hard negatives (first step).</b> Held-out intents are separable (oracle AUROC {{ n(p6a.d1.rows[0].unseen) }}) but the unsupervised score reaches {{ n(p6a.d1.maha) }}: generate out-of-scope messages that reuse keywords of the {{ n('eda.k') }} intents, keep those all three judges unanimously label as fitting none, and compare a K-plus-one class head against outlier exposure on the same Track B holdouts.</li>
<li><b>More labelled data.</b> The measured learning curve (D4): the AUROC slope is {{ n(p6a.d4.auroc_slope) }} per doubling of the training data, but the rejection slope ({{ n(p6a.d4.rej_slope) }}) has an interval reaching zero, so label abstained and low-margin traffic first.</li>
<li><b>An ID-consistency variant with its measured trade-off.</b> The consistency loss changed the neutral-swap flip rate by {{ n('p6a.ax.i4a.c') }} and {{ n('p6a.ax.i4b.c') }} against CV macro-F1 {{ n('p6a.ax.i4a.a_ci') }} and {{ n('p6a.ax.i4b.a_ci') }} (two loss weights); it needs a variant that recovers the F1 loss and must be guarded on Track B too.</li>
</ul>

</main>

