<p><b>What would break it.</b> (i) D1 is an upper bound: verified hard-negative data on classes never trained on (N1) is the test of whether the headroom of {{ n(p6a.d1.headroom) }} is reachable. (ii) D2 rules out the ID shortcut as the cause of the v1-versus-v3 ranking, not of closed-set accuracy riding on ID text (Appendix {{ sec.robust }}). (iii) Rejection differences below the D3 spread (sd {{ n(p6a.d3.rej_sd) }}) are noise unless both arms share the threshold rows, as in the paired bootstrap of the open-set improvement round. (iv) If the D4 rejection slope CI ({{ n(p6a.d4.rej_slope) }}) keeps reaching zero, more data of the same kind is not the lever for rejection.</p>

<h2>Selection History and the v1/v3 Decision</h2>
<p>{{ n('log.eval.distinct_final_fps') }} final models were trained and each was test-evaluated once ({{ M() }} single recorded evaluation, {{ n('hist.v1.f1') }} for v1, {{ n('hist.v2.f1') }} for v2, {{ n('hist.v3.f1') }} for v3: differences far inside the intervals). v2 (adds machine-translated and noisy copies of train rows, factor A3) was adopted under a rule that guarded Track A only, then reverted: on the scored Track B headline its strict rejection fell by {{ n('hist.v2.head.rej95') }} (paired), neutral-swap flips rose from {{ n('hist.v2.flip_cur') }} to {{ n('hist.v2.flip_cand') }}, and calibration temperature moved from {{ n('hist.v1.T') }} to {{ n('hist.v2.T') }}. Multi-axis selection then selected on several axes with several seeds; the selection rule, fixed before the candidates were run, picked v3 (A1+A3, epoch {{ n('hist.v3.epoch') }}). <b>Decision: v1 ships, overriding the rule's pick.</b> Reasons, in order: (a) the scored Track B headline regressed for v3 (table below); (b) v3's eligibility depended on v1 being read at its shipped epoch {{ n('hist.sens.v1_e') }}, a local dip (own best epoch {{ n('hist.sens.v1_argmax') }}; CV F1 {{ n('hist.sens.v1_f1_e') }} vs {{ n('hist.sens.v1_f1_arg') }}), and against the best epoch the outcome flips (same outcome: {{ t('hist.sens.same') }}); (c) the DEV axis was not predictive of the headline regression. Test macro-F1 played no part.</p>
<table class="split">
