<h2>Ablations and Bake-Off Detail</h2>
<p><b>Approach, in detail.</b> The task is single-label, {{ n('eda.k') }}-way intent routing on {{ n('eda.n') }} rows with a multilingual tail, plus an open-set requirement, so the system has two parts. First, a closed-set classifier: multilingual-e5-base fine-tuned end to end with the standard classification head (dense + tanh + linear) on the first token (learning rate {{ n('a.lr') }}, batch {{ n('a.batch') }}, max length {{ n('a.maxlen') }}, stopped at epoch {{ n('a.epoch') }} of a {{ n('a.epochs_sched') }}-epoch schedule, seed {{ n('a.model_seed') }}), with temperature scaling fitted on validation rows. Second, a post-hoc open-set score on its penultimate features (Mahalanobis distance to the class means) whose threshold is set on known-class validation rows only, so that {{ n('srv.ret_target') }} of known rows are kept; messages below it go to an unknown path instead of a handler. Floors: B0 (character TF-IDF + LR) and B1 (frozen multilingual-e5-base embeddings + LR). Candidates (all <code>AutoModelForSequenceClassification</code>): multilingual-e5-base, xlm-roberta-base, mdeberta-v3-base (learning rate swept per model, then {{ n('bk.e5_lr3e-05.n') }} fold-runs for the best). Rule fixed before any result: highest mean CV macro-F1; a smaller or faster model within one std wins; top two compared with the Nadeau-Bengio corrected t-test.</p>
